<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch NPM buys 8.15 pct of PolyDoc.</title>
<headline>Dutch NPM buys 8.15 pct of PolyDoc.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Information management software firm PolyDoc Plc said on Thursday venture capital firm Nederlandse Participatie Maatschappij NV (NPM) had bought an 8.15 percent stake in it for one million stg.</p>
<p>PolyDoc is based in Amsterdam but launched 4.6 million of its shares on London's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) last September. NPM has taken up about one third of this issue and the other shares were bought by British investors.</p>
<p>PolyDoc previously said it would use the proceeds of the share issue to finance future growth.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
